        <div class="explain">
          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>Four groups the survey counts separately from the SC, ST and OBC figures above: Persons With Disability, Muslims, Other Minority Communities, and the newer EWS category. Each group has two bars: men (grey) above, women (blue) below. These are counts: how many enrolled, not how large the group is. A small bar may mean a small community or a community that college reaches poorly: the survey serves no denominator to tell them apart.</p>
            <p>The gender split within each group is its own signal. Muslims reach near-parity (women are half of Muslim enrolment); disability enrolment skews male, as disability identification itself does. EWS is the youngest category, its line in the data begins in 2020-21, after the reservation came in, so no trend is drawn for it yet.</p>
