  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Ministry of Education, Department of Higher Education. All India Survey on Higher Education (AISHE), survey rounds 2017-18 to 2021-22: the five rounds the eSankhyiki API serves. Retrieved via the MoSPI eSankhyiki API, vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>. The survey itself runs to 2010-11; earlier rounds are not chained in, because the institutional frame widened over time and a longer line would mix survey-coverage gains with genuine expansion.</p>
        <p>Coverage: all nine AISHE indicators are ingested raw and baked, every one by state as well as for All India; thirteen bundles carry the page and the table of every cut. The headline series (universities, colleges, enrolment, teachers, GER, GPI, PTR), the access cuts (GER by social category × gender, GPI by social category, enrolment by gender), the composition (enrolment by education level and social group), the state grain (enrolment, GER and GPI by state/UT), the faculty hierarchy (teachers by the five regular faculty types × gender) and the minority cut (PWD &amp; minority enrolment by gender). Nothing is selected away: every indicator the survey publishes is on the page or in the audit dump behind it.</p>
        <p><b>A correction, October 2026.</b> Version 1.0 of this guide said the survey's 2021-22 "All Teacher" total was garbled (12,904 for All India) and rebuilt it from the five regular posts. That was our error, not the survey's: the download of 9 August 2026 came back from the API in an unstable page order, which repeated some rows and dropped others. A clean download on 10 October 2026, checked row by row for repeats, shows the published total, 15,97,688 teachers, and shows it equal to the five regular posts plus visiting teachers in 546 of 549 state, year and gender cells (All India 2020-21 is 34 teachers apart). Nagaland's 2021-22 enrolment, missing before, also returned. Every download is now checked for repeated rows and fails if it finds one. Both dumps are kept in the audit trail.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>AISHE results are final on release. The five rounds are comparable by design but are never chained into a spliced index. Enrolment counts enrolments, not distinct students; GER divides by a population projection; GPI is a ratio of ratios. Where a figure is corrected, the correction is disclosed and the earlier download is kept. Where something is not measured, completion, dropout, learning, this guide says so.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Education, version 1.2 (October 2026). Version 1.1 added GER by gender (§07), the state enrolment companion strip (§08), the education-level small multiples (§09), the faculty-hierarchy plate (§10) and the PWD &amp; minority plate (§11). Version 1.2 bakes every indicator by state, adds the state plates on teachers, women and colleges (§13), and corrects the 2021-22 teacher total (see above). Next scheduled revision: on release of the 2022-23 round.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
